  "name": "Test Quadruped",
  "class": "large_prop",
  "_note": "Four legs on a body, and the fixture that holds down the sentence RIG-SPEC §4 spends a paragraph on: a human knee points forward and a horse's hock points backward, and the difference is read off the rest pose rather than declared. The forelegs' shins jog 2 modules FORWARD of their thighs, so their `bend` comes out -Z; the hind legs' jog 2 modules BACKWARD, so theirs comes out +Z. Same code, opposite answer, no field. Whole modules and right angles throughout, as `leg.json` and `biped.json` are.",
  "_asymmetric": "The front and back legs are deliberately different lengths, and not for looks. `Locomotion._measure` takes `drop` as the MINIMUM across the legs — the most constrained leg is what decides how far the body may ride above the lowest foot — and a fixture whose legs all had the same drop could not tell a minimum from a maximum. Forelegs: span 2.8, hip at 2.4, drop 0.4. Hind legs: span 2.6, hip at 2.0, drop 0.6. So `drop` is 0.4, and a `_measure` that took the maximum would say 0.6.",
  "_derived": "Foreleg: hip (±0.3, 2.4, -0.9), knee (±0.3, 1.2, -1.1), ankle (±0.3, 0, -1.1), sole (±0.3, 0, -1.5); span 2.8, reach = 2.8 - sqrt(6.12) = 0.3261. Hind leg: hip (±0.3, 2.0, 0.9), knee (±0.3, 0.8, 1.1), ankle (±0.3, 0, 1.1), sole (±0.3, 0, 0.5); span 2.6, reach = 2.6 - sqrt(4.16) = 0.5604. Every sole sits at y = 0, so stand = 0.",
